[meta]
lang: en
title: OireMark conformance tests: Code Blocks
[/meta]

h1. Code Blocks

Tests for Section 10 of the specification.

h2. Bracket Form

h3. Bracket form with language {#code-bracket-language}
```om
[code python]
def hello():
    print("Hello, world!")
[/code]
```
[code html]
<pre><code class="language-python">def hello():
    print("Hello, world!")
</code></pre>
[/code]

h3. Bracket form without language {#code-bracket-plain}
```om
[code]
plain text
[/code]
```
[code html]
<pre><code>plain text
</code></pre>
[/code]

h3. Content is literal {#code-bracket-literal}
```om
[code]
*not bold* \[not escaped\] <b>not html</b>
h2. Not a heading
[/code]
```
[code html]
<pre><code>*not bold* \[not escaped\] &lt;b&gt;not html&lt;/b&gt;
h2. Not a heading
</code></pre>
[/code]

h3. Indentation and blank lines are preserved {#code-bracket-whitespace}
```om
[code]
first

    indented
[/code]
```
[code html]
<pre><code>first

    indented
</code></pre>
[/code]

h3. A closing tag in the middle of a line is content {#code-bracket-close-mid-line}
```om
[code]
x [/code] y
[/code]
```
[code html]
<pre><code>x [/code] y
</code></pre>
[/code]

h3. Empty code block {#code-bracket-empty}
```om
[code]
[/code]
```
[code html]
<pre><code></code></pre>
[/code]

h3. An indented closing tag closes the block {#code-bracket-indented-close}
```om
[code]
x
    [/code]
```
[code html]
<pre><code>x
</code></pre>
[/code]

h3. Unclosed bracket form {#code-bracket-unclosed}
[code om]
[code]
never closed
[/code]
[code error]
unclosed-block 1
[/code]

h2. Fenced Form

h3. Fenced form with language {#code-fenced-language}
[code om]
```python
def hello():
    print("Hello, world!")
```
[/code]
[code html]
<pre><code class="language-python">def hello():
    print("Hello, world!")
</code></pre>
[/code]

h3. Fenced form without language {#code-fenced-plain}
[code om]
```
plain text
```
[/code]
[code html]
<pre><code>plain text
</code></pre>
[/code]

h3. A longer fence can contain a shorter one {#code-fenced-nested}
[code om]
````
```
This fence is part of the content.
```
````
[/code]
[code html]
<pre><code>```
This fence is part of the content.
```
</code></pre>
[/code]

h3. The closing fence may be longer than the opening one {#code-fenced-longer-close}
[code om]
```
x
`````
[/code]
[code html]
<pre><code>x
</code></pre>
[/code]

h3. A backtick line with text after it does not close the fence {#code-fenced-info-not-closing}
[code om]
```
```python
```
[/code]
[code html]
<pre><code>```python
</code></pre>
[/code]

h3. Unclosed fence {#code-fenced-unclosed}
[code om]
Text.

```
never closed
[/code]
[code error]
unclosed-block 3
[/code]

h3. A shorter fence does not close a longer one {#code-fenced-shorter-not-closing}
[code om]
````
x
```
[/code]
[code error]
unclosed-block 1
[/code]

h3. The fenced form shows a literal closing tag {#code-fenced-literal-close-tag}
````om
```
[code]
x
[/code]
```
````
```html
<pre><code>[code]
x
[/code]
</code></pre>
```

h2. Profiles

h3. Code blocks are not allowed in the inline profile {#code-profile-inline}
; profile
: inline
```om
[code]
x
[/code]
```
[code error]
feature-not-in-profile 1
[/code]
